# Flutter-related
**/Flutter/ephemeral/
**/Pods/

# CocoaPods, regenerated by `pod install` on every macOS build.
#
# `Pods/` was already here; these two were not, so every build left them sitting
# untracked in `git status` — and scripts/release-desktop.sh refuses to tag a
# dirty tree, which is correct and meant every release had to step around them.
# Flutter writes both deterministically from the plugin list, so there is nothing
# in them a checkout cannot reproduce.
Podfile
Podfile.lock

